1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,000
AI is no longer just chat.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,500
It is reading business data, analyzing operations,
calling tools, and even modifying business systems.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:13,500
When AI starts to act,
the missing piece is not a smarter agent.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,000
It is trust.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
KeelBase is an open-source
Enterprise AI Trust Runtime.
It connects AI agents with real business systems.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Upstream: MCP, OpenAPI, Function Calling, existing agents.
Downstream: CRM, ERP, OA, and legacy systems.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:45,000
In between, KeelBase keeps every AI business action
inside explicit boundaries.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
In KeelBase, AI does more than answer questions.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,000
It reads real business data
and analyzes it with business rules.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Here, AI finds a high-risk customer
and explains where the risk comes from.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:14,000
But analysis and execution are different.
Reading can happen. Business writes cannot happen silently.

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Creating a task is a business side effect,
so KeelBase requires explicit user confirmation.

13
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Only after approval does AI actually modify the CRM.
This is not a simulated answer.

14
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Business data has really changed.

15
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Enterprises need to know: why did AI decide this?
Who initiated it? Why was it allowed? Who approved it?

16
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:58,000
KeelBase records the full decision and audit trail,
and verifies its integrity with a hash chain.

17
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:06,000
AI side effects are not "once it happens, it is over."

18
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:12,000
For supported operations, KeelBase can track
and revoke business records created by AI.

19
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,000
AI actions become controllable and correctable.

20
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:25,000
This is what makes KeelBase different
from a typical agent framework.

21
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:35,000
It provides a trust layer between AI and business.
AI can reach real systems, but cannot bypass boundaries.

22
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:42,000
What if AI tries to go beyond the user's data scope?

23
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Permission is enforced at runtime.
Even if AI makes the request, it must pass authorization.
A denial is not an anomaly. It is the system working.

24
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:55,000
These security boundaries are not slogans.
They are executable validations that ship with the codebase.

25
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:03,000
KeelBase does not only run AI.
It also helps developers build AI applications.

26
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Describe the business contract with an Application Protocol,
and AI generates real application code.

27
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:22,000
The output is normal, readable, editable source code.
Not a low-code black box that locks you into the platform.

28
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Enterprises do not need to start over.
KeelBase bridges existing databases, OpenAPI, or Java systems.

29
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Ten-year-old business systems gain AI capability
without being rebuilt.

30
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:53,000
For sensitive businesses, KeelBase supports Docker,
offline, and local model deployment.

31
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Data can stay in your environment,
while AI still does real business work.

32
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Build. Run. Trust. Private Deploy.
AI can act, but only within explicit business boundaries.
